      "title": "French police officers found guilty of racist assault on black music producer",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/20/french-police-officers-found-guilty-of-racist-assault-on-black-music-producer",
      "description": "<p>Beating of Michel Zecler in 2020 sparked outrage over police brutality after it was caught on security cameras</p><p>Three French police officers who beat a black music producer they said was not wearing a face mask during the Covid pandemic have been found guilty of intentional, racist violence.</p><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/09/french-police-officers-face-trial-over-beating-of-black-man-not-wearing-mask-during-covid\">brutal assault</a> on Michel Zecler, now 47, was caught on security cameras in his building in 2020 and triggered outrage in France over police brutality. The trial this month was considered a turning point for the recognition of racist violence.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/20/french-police-officers-found-guilty-of-racist-assault-on-black-music-producer\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T22:23:53"
    },
